      "hash": "9c4f6579edd86b016143c774f6a88d814b06731bd5bb3279b303174d4d205cfc",
      "deps": [
        "thermo-2.9",
        "thermo-1.15"
      ],
      "idea": "Along a reversible path the first law gives $\\delta Q_{\\text{rev}} = dU + P\\,dV = nC_V\\,dT + nRT\\,dV/V$; dividing by $T$ leaves an exact differential (2.9) that integrates at once. Constant $S$ means $C_V\\ln T + R\\ln V$ fixed, i.e. $TV^{R/C_V} = TV^{\\gamma - 1}$ fixed: reversible adiabats are isentropes, which is why \"adiabatic\" and \"isentropic\" are used interchangeably for quasistatic processes. Raising $T$ or $V$ raises $S$ \u2014 more energy to share, more room to share it in."
    },
