      "hash": "030dfd5299a8dc75b036aa76ba172de616433f0fafd227644c4e69ff5cf47468",
      "deps": [
        "thermo-3.3"
      ],
      "idea": "Differentiate the homogeneity identity with respect to $\\lambda$ and set $\\lambda = 1$ (Euler's theorem on homogeneous functions): $S = U\\,\\partial_U S + V\\,\\partial_V S + N\\,\\partial_N S$, and the partial derivatives are $1/T$, $P/T$, $-\\mu/T$ (3.2). Geometrically, $\\lambda \\mapsto S(\\lambda X)$ is a straight line through the origin, so its tangent at $\\lambda = 1$ \u2014 whose slope is the right-hand side \u2014 passes through the origin too. The thermodynamic identity (3.3) then \"integrates\" to the Euler form because $T$, $P$, $\\mu$ stay fixed as the system is scaled."
    },
